## Rebuttal
1. fixed — takeHeavySlot takes a `slots()` thunk and refuses any result that is not an integer 1..64 before trying a slot past 1 (Interfaces, row 5a, b2 row). Other instances: runInHeavySlot shares the same loop.
2. fixed — an inherited lease is reused for slot-1..slot-64 whatever the reader's own capacity (Interfaces, row 4, b2 capacity-mismatch row), so a nested reader with a different heavy_job_slots never waits on its own lease.
3. fixed for npm test, narrowed for in-process owners — the wrapper runs its command under `flock <slot> sh -c … exec "$@"`, so the command holds the locked file open (flock-fd-inherit.txt) and killing the wrapper does not free the slot (b3 row). For ci/verify/run, killing the owner alone frees the slot while children it started run on; stated as a limit under Promise host-cap (a capacity gap, no gate passes).
4. fixed — after `held`, a helper exit prints `heavy-job: slot lost` and changes nothing else; the error clause applies only before `held` (Interfaces, row 5, host-cap limit, b2 row).
5. fixed — missing flock refuses with the entry point's refusal code: 2, or 1 for runBuilderCommand (Promise freed-on-death, Interfaces).
6. fixed — Promise outcome-kept narrowed: pass/fail and timeouts kept; a reused lease prints nothing, so verify's test-gate log (packages/pipeline/src/index.ts:96 status line) is unchanged; a taken slot adds heavy-job: stderr lines, and the wrapper reports a signal as 128+N.
7. fixed — capacity is read only when slot 1 is busy, so on a fresh runner the wrapper reads no studio/ file under record-reads.mjs (.github/workflows/ci.yml:72-77); row 10 says so, and row 2 states that a bad value is then caught by checkStudio, not at run time.
8. fixed — row 12 names runCi's reused `npm test` subprocess and runStep's exit (packages/commands/src/ci.ts:114-121).
9. fixed — row 13 names runBuilderCommand's reused host runner and its status/result-file rejector (packages/commands/src/builder-run.ts:215-230).
